('alict_01006', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which storage medium was known for its ability to hold large amounts of data but required sequential access?', '["Magnetic Tape", "Solid-State Drives", "Optical Discs", "Hard drive", "Pen Drive"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Magnetic tape is a storage medium that can hold large amounts of data but is known for requiring sequential access. This means that to retrieve specific the tape has to be read from the beginning until the required data is making it slower com pared to modern storage systems', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1006, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01007', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which port is commonly used for connecting high-definition displays and supports both audio and video signals?', '["USB-C According to this it is false. USB -C is versatile and supports both data transfer and video signals. it is not specifically designed for high -definition displays. While it can transmit audio and it is primarily used for other purposes like charging and connecting devices", "DVI According to this it is false. DVI (Digital Visual Interface) is used for transmitting video signals but does not support audio. It is primarily for video output and does not fully meet the needs for high- definition displays with both video and audio signals", "DisplayPort According to this it is true. DisplayPort is designed to connect high -definition displays and supports both audio and video signals. It is commonly used in modern computers and monitors to transmit high-definition making it the correct answer", "PS", "Serial port According to this it is false. A serial port is mainly used for communication between devices and does not handle video or audio making it irrelevant to connecting high-definition displays. fuu th flfjkshla m%Odk ix{d yiqrejkafka th"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "USB-C According to this it is false. USB -C is versatile and supports both data transfer and video signals. it is not specifically designed for high -definition displays. While it can transmit audio and it is primarily used for other purposes like charging and connecting devices". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1007, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01008', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What causes images to appear on a CRT monitor?', '["An electron beam striking a phosphorescent surface. fmdiamria", "Electrical impulses sent directly to the pixels", "Light-emitting diodes arranged on the surface", "Liquid crystals manipulated by electric current", "Plasma gas reactions within the monitor"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: as described above. Option 2: Incorrect. This applies to some flat-screen not Option 3: Incorrect. Light Emitting Diodes are used in modern LED monitors. Option 4: Incorrect. This describes LCD not Option 5: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1008, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01009', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is a primary goal of Time -Sharing Operating Systems compared to Multi - Programmed Batch Systems?', '["Maximizing CPU utilization by keeping multiple jobs in switching between them efficiently. nyq", "Providing an interactive environment where users can directly interact with the system and receive immediate feedback", "Minimizing the turnaround time for batch jobs by executing them sequentially without any user intervention", "Reducing the number of jobs in the system to avoid context switching and overhead", "Ensuring that the system does not have any idle time by using batch processing techniques"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Providing an interactive environment where users can directly interact with the system and receive immediate feedback". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1009, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01010', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following monitor has the best energy efficiency and color accuracy?', '["CRT monitor", "TFT monitor", "LED monitor", "Plasma monitor", "LCD monitor"]'::jsonb, 3, 'CRT Monitor Consumes high power and outdated technology. 2) TFT Monitor A type of LCD that is energy-efficient but not as much as LED monitors. 3) LED Monitor Combines the energy efficiency of with enhanced color accuracy and brightness using LED backlighting', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1010, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
