('alict_01017', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not true about time sharing operating systems?', '["They enhance resource utilization by sharing resources", "They allocate CPU time slices to multiple users. nyq", "They rely on context switching to manage sessions. ieis", "They provide quick response times for interactive tasks", "A single user can monopolize the CPU for long periods"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: True. Time-sharing operating systems are designed to improve resource utilization by allowing multiple users to share resources effectively. fnod bv Option 2: True. Time-sharing systems allocate CPU time in small slices to different ensuring fair access. Option 3: True', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1017, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
