('alict_01033', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What happens during a context switch in a multitasking operating system?', '["The CPU forgets all information about the currently running program. CPU oekg", "The operating system saves the state of the current program and loads the state of a new program", "The CPU allocates more memory to the currently running program. CPU oekg", "The operating system terminates the currently running program", "The operating system increases the clock speed of the CPU"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In a multitasking operating a context switch occurs when the operating system switches the CPU from one process or task to another', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1033, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01034', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements best describes preemptive scheduling?', '["The CPU scheduler picks a process to run and allows it to finish before picking another process. CPU kshuldrlh", "A process is only replaced if it voluntarily relinquishes the CPU", "The CPU scheduler may interrupt a currently running process to assign the CPU to another process. CPU kshuldrlh", "Processes run to completion without any interruptions", "The operating system switches processes only when the current process ends its time quantum"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In preemptive the operating system can pause a currently running process to give CPU time to another ensuring better resource management and especially in multi -tasking environments', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1034, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01035', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the scheduler which selects processes from secondary storage device?', '["Short term scheduler", "Medium term scheduler", "Process scheduler", "Long term scheduler", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Long term scheduler". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1035, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
