('alict_01037', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is a function of the Memory Management Unit (MMU) in a computer system?', '["Managing the speed of the CPU", "Converting logical addresses to physical addresses", "Managing the power consumption of the", "Handling the network connections", "Controlling input and output devices"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) Converting logical addresses to physical addresses. The Memory Management Unit (MMU) is responsible for translating logical (virtual) addresses used by programs into physical addresses that correspond to locations in the actual hardware memory (RAM)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1037, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
