('alict_01039', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is a key difference between a long -term scheduler and a short -term scheduler in an operating system?', '["The long-term scheduler controls the degree of while the short-term scheduler selects processes to run on the CPU", "The long-term scheduler switches processes from the ready state to the running while the short- term scheduler manages input", "The short-term scheduler is also known as Job scheduler while long-term scheduler also known as CPU scheduler", "The long-term scheduler operates while the short-term scheduler operates occasionally", "The short-term scheduler manages the creation of while the long-term scheduler deals with their termination"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "The long-term scheduler controls the degree of while the short-term scheduler selects processes to run on the CPU". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1039, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01040', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is a key characteristic of a Peer-to-Peer (P2P) network model?', '["A powerful centralized server manages all resources", "Peer devices act as both clients and servers. iu fiajdodhlhska fiajdodhlhka", "Communication occurs exclusively between a client and a server", "It is restricted to small geographical areas like homes or offices. th ksjdi", "Only servers can share resources with peers. iu"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A key characteristic of a Peer -to-Peer (P2P) network model is that peer devices act as both clients and servers. In this type of each device (peer) can request resources (acting as a client) and provide resources (acting as a server) simultaneousl y', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1040, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
