('alict_01051', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the primary function of a NIC (Network Interface Card) in an ICT system?', '["Encrypting data for cybersecurity", "Translating programming languages into machine code", "Connecting a computer to a network", "Managing memory allocation for programs", "Assigning IP addresses to networking devices"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Encryption is handled by security protocols SSL (Trusted Platform Modules). yiqrejkq ,nkafka SSL Option 2: Incorrect. This is done by compilers or interpreters. Option 3: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1051, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01052', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following best describes an expert system?', '["A type of software used to generate random numbers for statistical analysis", "A system that uses machine learning to improve its performance based on user feedback", "A software application designed to mimic the decision-making abilities of a human expert in a specific domain", "A hardware device that accelerates data processing for large-scale simulations. uyd simulations", "A network of computers that work together to share resources and manage data"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A software application designed to mimic the decision-making abilities of a human expert in a specific domain". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1052, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01053', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'A small educational institution has few computers in a computer lab. They need a simple and low-cost network to share resources like printers and the internet. The network doesn''t need to be complex. The institution doesn''t expect to add more devices lsysmhla fnod Tjqkag wvq blaukska fkdlrhs'' Which network topology is the best fit for this scenario?', '["Star topology", "Mesh topology", "Tree topology", "Bus topology", "Ring topology"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The best network topology for this scenario is Bus topology. In a bus all computers are connected to a single central cable which reduces the cost and complexity of wiring. This is a simple and low-cost making it ideal for smaller networks like the one described', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1053, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01054', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the maximum number of IP addresses that can be assigned to hosts on a subnet with a subnet mask of 255.255.255.224?', '["14", "30", "62", "126", "254"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "30". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1054, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01055', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the main purpose of a network switch?', '["To provide internet access by converting digital signals into analog", "To boost weak signals and extend network coverage", "To connect multiple devices and manage data traffic efficiently within a network lsysmhla", "To connect different networks based on IP addresses. IP", "To act as a gateway between wired and wireless networks"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. This function is performed by a not a switch. Option 2: Incorrect. A not a is used to amplify weak signals. Option 3: Correct. A switch connects multiple devices in a network and directs data packets efficiently based on MAC addresses', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1055, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01056', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following layers in the TCP', '["Application Layer", "Transport Layer", "Network Layer", "Data Link Layer", "Session Layer"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The Transport Layer (TCP sequence and retransmission. It maps to the Transport layer (Layer 4) in the OSI model. (TCP', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1056, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01057', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'The transmission data rate is decided', '["Transport layer", "Network layer", "Data link layer", "Physical layer", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The transmission data also known as the bit is indeed determined by the Physical layer (Layer 1) of the OSI model. u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1057, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01058', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which unit is commonly used to measure bandwidth?', '["Bytes", "Bits per second (bps)", "Megabytes (MB)", "Hertz (Hz)", "Rounds per minute (Rpm)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The unit commonly used to measure bandwidth is 2) Bits per second (bps). Bandwidth refers to the maximum rate of data transfer across a network or internet connection', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1058, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01059', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following is true about addressing in ,sms fhduq MAC addresses are globally unique and assigned by manufacturers. MAC ksIamdolhska IP addresses can be changed by software u.ska IP yel'' C. MAC addresses are used at the Network Layer', '["A and D only A D", "and D only B D", "B and C only B C", "A and B only A B", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Statement True. MAC (Media Access Control) addresses are typically assigned by hardware manufacturers and are intended to be globally unique. These addresses are hardcoded into the network interface card (NIC) and operate at the Data Link Layer (Layer 2) of the OSI model', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1059, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01060', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'National Internet Service Provider (ISP) networks are connected to one another by private switching network is', '["Peering Points", "Network Access Points", "National ISP", "Data Centers", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Peering Points Peering points are locations where different Internet Service Providers (ISPs) connect and exchange traffic directly with each other. This direct connection allows for the efficient and cost-effective transfer of data without having to pass through a third-party network', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1060, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01061', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'An organization with a network of branches all over the island has prepared to install a new system to replace the old customer management system in its organization. It will be established in the existing branch in Colombo and only if it is it will be established in other branches as well. What kind of system deployment is this?', '["Direct deployment", "Parallel deployment", "Phased deployment", "Pilot deployment", "Automated deployment"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Pilot deployment". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1061, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01062', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following statements is true about the difference between a hub and a switch?', '["A hub sends data only to the intended while a switch broadcasts to all", "Switches cannot handle full-duplex communication", "A switch operates at the data link layer", "Hubs are faster and more intelligent than switches", "Both hub and switch work at the transport layer"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. It''s actually the opposite. A hub broadcasts to all while a switch sends data only to the intended device using MAC addresses. th Option 2: This is incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1062, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01063', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following statements about addresses is false?', '["The most commonly used loopback IP address in systems is 127.0.0.1", "The loopback interface is connected to localhost. loopback", "The network address to which an IP address belongs is set to 0, which identifies all hosts. IP ,smskhla", "The network address to which an IP address belongs is set to 0, which identifies all networks. IP ,smskhla", "All IP addresses from 127.0.0.0 to 127.255.255.255 are reserved for loopback interfaces. 127.0.0.0 isg 127.255.255.255 IP"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: is indeed the most commonly used loopback which refers to the local machine for testing purposes. Option 2: The loopback interface refers to the virtual network interface that is used to connect to the local machine commonly known as localhost', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1063, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01064', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Consider a network application that requires low can tolerate some data and does not require packet order enforcement. Which transport layer protocol is most and why?', '["because it provides ordered delivery of all packets TCP th", "because it is connectionless and has lower allowing faster transmission UDP ukao th", "because it supports flow control and congestion management TCP ukao th", "because it guarantees delivery but not order UDP ukao th", "because it operates at the physical layer for speed ukao th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) is reliable and ensures all packets arrive in order. It also has error flow and congestion but this adds overhead and latency', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1064, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01065', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which statement about network security is correct?', '["Firewalls are used to encrypt data on a network", "Antivirus software is used to prevent unauthorized access to a network", "Encryption is used to convert data into a code to prevent unauthorized access. wkjir", "Authentication ensures that data is not altered during transmission", "Intrusion detection systems are used to physically protect network devices"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Encryption is used to convert data into a code to prevent unauthorized access. wkjir". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1065, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01066', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following is an example of a network topology?', '["Star", "Circle", "Sphere", "Node", "Hub"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Star". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1066, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01067', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the primary purpose of edge computing in applications?', '["To centralize data processing in cloud", "To reduce latency by processing data closer to the", "To enhance security through", "To increase bandwidth for data", "To manage user interfaces more"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Real-time processing Many applications demand immediate responses to events or data changes. By processing data at the closer to the delay between data generation and processing is significantly reduced. This enables faster decision-making and more efficient operations', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1067, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01068', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following is the protocol that is used to prevent data collision in the Ring topology?', '["CSMA", "Token Ring", "ALOHA", "Slotted ALOHA", "Telnet"]'::jsonb, 2, 'CSMA This protocol is used in Ethernet where devices can sense the carrier signal and detect collisions. It does not apply to ring topologies', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1068, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01069', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What does the tracert command do in a networking context?', '["It tests the reachability of a host", "It displays the path taken by packets to a destination. th", "It configures network interfaces", "It measures the bandwidth of a connection", "It retrieves the IP address of a domain name"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The tracert command (short for "trace route") is used to trace the route that packets take from the source to a destination host in a network. It provides information about each node along the including the time it takes for packets to travel to each helping diagnose network issues', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1069, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01070', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following IP addresses is not a Class D IP address?', '["224.0.10.1", "243.0.10.1", "230.20.10.67", "233.233.233.233", "225.0.54.5"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Class D IP addresses are used for multicast groups and range from 224.0.0.0 to 239.255.255.255. Let''s analyze each of the given IP addresses to determine which one is not a Class D olajd mrdihl Let''s go through the given options 1) 224.0.10', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1070, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01071', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following is not a commonly used network topology?', '["Star topology", "Mesh topology", "Ring topology", "Line topology", "Tree topology"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Star Topology Star topology is a widely used network topology where each node (computer or device) is connected to a central hub or switch. The hub acts as a central point of managing data traffic between the nodes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1071, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01072', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'A = Session Layer - ieis = Transport Layer - = Presentation Layer - = Data Link Layer - = Application Layer - = Physical Layer - = Network Layer - is the correct order of the above layers for the OSI data transmission model?', '["ECBDAGF", "DGECABF", "FDCGABE", "ECABGDF", "CFABEDG"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) model is a conceptual framework used to understand and describe how different networking protocols and technologies interact to facilitate communication between devices in a network', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1072, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01073', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the network address for the IP 192.168.5.130 with a subnet mask of', '["192.168.5.0", "192.168.5.128", "192.168.5.64", "192.168.5.192", "255.255.255.128 Answer"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Step 1: A /25 subnet mask means 25 bits are used for the network and the remaining 7 bits are for hosts (32 - 25 = 7). /25 - 25 = 7). This gives 2⁷ = 128 total IP addresses per subnet. Step 2: We calculate the subnet First subnet 192.168.5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1073, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01074', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which device operates at the Data Link layer of the OSI model?', '["Router", "Hub", "Switch", "Repeater", "Firewall"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A router operates at the Network layer (Layer 3) of the OSI model. It routes data between different networks and determines the best path for data to travel. rjqgrhla OSI 2) A hub operates at the Physical layer (Layer 1) of the OSI model', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1074, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01075', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following statements is true about the OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) model?', '["The Network layer is responsible for and terminating connections between applications", "The Data Link layer is responsible for end-to-end communication and error correction across the entire network", "The Transport layer provides reliable data transfer services to the upper layers and is responsible for flow and error recovery", "The Presentation layer handles the routing of data packets between different networks and subnets", "The Session layer is responsible for packet forwarding including routing through intermediate routers"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "The Transport layer provides reliable data transfer services to the upper layers and is responsible for flow and error recovery". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1075, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01076', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'A university wants to separate its Wi-Fi network for students and while still connecting both to the internet. Which device is MOST responsible for managing this traffic separation?', '["Repeater", "Hub", "Router", "Switch", "Modem"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A router is responsible for separating and managing traffic between different networks student Wi-Fi and staff Wi-Fi) while still providing access to the internet. rjqgrhla A switch only separates devices within the same network (LAN), not different networks', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1076, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01077', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following statements about data transmission methods is most accurate and multicasting?', '["Unicasting sends data to a single destination while broadcasting sends data to all devices on the and multicasting sends data to a specific group of devices. Unicasting", "Broadcasting is the most efficient method for sending data to a large number of devices on a network", "Multicasting requires special network protocols but offers better efficiency than unicasting for sending data to a group of devices. nyq", "All network devices can send and receive data using broadcasting and multicasting methods", "Unicasting is the only method that guarantees reliable delivery of data to the destination device. Unicasting"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Unicasting sends data to a single destination while broadcasting sends data to all devices on the and multicasting sends data to a specific group of devices. Unicasting". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1077, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01078', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'In which of the following describes a secure method for verifying customer identity during transactions?', '["Username and Password", "IP Address Tracking", "One Time Password", "Cookies", "Simple Click Agreement"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: While commonly this method alone is not considered highly secure because passwords can be stolen or guessed. wkqudk yels Option 2: This is not a reliable method for verifying as IP addresses can change or be spoofed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1078, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01079', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What does the term "bandwidth" refer to in networking?', '["The physical distance between devices in a network", "The amount of data that can be transmitted in a fixed amount of time", "The number of devices connected to a network", "The type of cables used in a network", "The security level of a network"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The term bandwidth in networking refers to the amount of data that can be transmitted over a network in a fixed amount of time. It is usually measured in bits per second (bps), kilobits per second megabits per second or gigabits per second', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1079, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01080', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following commands is issued to identify that which computer or router not functioning as expected in a computer network?', '["Netstat", "Ping", "IPConfig", "Tracert", "Hostname"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Tracert". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1080, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
