('alict_01201', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the correct SQL statement used to return only different values?', '["SELECT DIFFERENT", "SELECT ONLY", "SELECT NULL", "SELECT CHECK", "SELECT DISTINCT"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "SELECT DISTINCT". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1201, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01202', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL clause is used to restrict the number of rows returned by a query?', '["WHERE", "GROUP BY", "ORDER BY", "LIMIT", "DISTINCT"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Used to filter rows based on specific conditions but does not restrict the number of rows returned. Option 2: Used to group rows that have the same values in specified columns. It does not limit the number of rows returned', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1202, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01203', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL statement is used to modify existing records in a table?', '["INSERT", "UPDATE", "DELETE", "SELECT", "ALTER"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Used to add new records to a table 2) Used to modify or change existing records in a table. 3) Used to remove records from a table 4) Used to retrieve data from a database 5) Used to modify the structure of a table (e.g', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1203, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01204', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following is true about a foreign key?', '["It must have the same data type as the referenced primary key. thg fhduq ,o", "It can reference a non-unique column in the parent table. thg", "It can be null even if the referenced primary key is not null. fhduq ,o", "It can reference multiple columns in the parent table. thg", "It is not required to have an index. th"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A foreign key establishes a relationship between two tables by referencing a primary key in the parent table. To ensure consistency and data the foreign key must have the same data type as the referenced primary key', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1204, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01205', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the purpose of the DISTINCT keyword in SQL?', '["To sort the results in ascending order", "To return unique values from the selected column(s)", "To filter records with null values", "To count the number of records", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In the DISTINCT keyword is used to eliminate duplicate values from the result set and only return unique values in the specified column(s). It helps ensure that each value appears only once in the output. SQL DISTINCT moh nj', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1205, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01206', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL query retrieves only the most expensive videogame in the table?', '["SELECT Game_Name FROM Games ORDER BY Price ASC LIMIT", "SELECT Game_Name FROM Games ORDER BY Price", "SELECT * FROM Games WHERE Price = (SELECT MAX(Price) FROM", "SELECT * FROM Games ORDER BY Price", "SELECT MAX(Price) FROM"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "SELECT * FROM Games WHERE Price = (SELECT MAX(Price) FROM". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1206, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01207', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL query will return the total number of video games available in the store?', '["SELECT COUNT(Game_Name) FROM", "SELECT SUM(Game_Name) FROM", "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM Games WHERE Price", "SELECT COUNT(Platform) FROM", "SELECT MAX(Game_Name) FROM"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "SELECT COUNT(Game_Name) FROM". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1207, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01208', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following best describes the impact of the following SQL command?', '["Removes the table structure but retains the data for recovery. j.=", "Removes both the table structure and the data permanently. j.=", "Deletes the database that contains the employees table. fiajl wvx.=", "Temporarily hides the table but does not remove it from the database", "Deletes only indexes associated with the employees table. fiajl"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. The table''s structure and data are permanently not retained. Option 2: Correct according to the above explanation. Option 3: Incorrect. This command does not delete the only the table employees', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1208, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01209', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the correct SQL code to delete all rows from a table named Employee without dropping the table?', '["DELETE TABLE", "DROP TABLE", "REMOVE * FROM", "DELETE FROM", "CLEAR TABLE"]'::jsonb, 4, 'DELETE TABLE Incorrect because there is no such syntax in SQL. The correct syntax is DELETE FROM. SQL tjeks LKavhla 2) DROP TABLE Incorrect because DROP TABLE removes the entire including its structure and from the database', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1209, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01210', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following commands modifies the structure of a table?', '["A only. A", "A and C only. A C", "A and D only. A D", "C only. C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A. ALTER TABLE this command is specifically designed to modify the structure of a table. Examples of changes include • Adding or dropping columns. • Modifying data types of existing columns. • Adding or dropping constraints. ALTER TABLE Employees ADD COLUMN Age B', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1210, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01211', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following is a disadvantage of normalization?', '["It increases data redundancy", "It can lead to an increase in the number of tables", "It reduces query performance by creating fewer joins. th wvq", "It complicates the schema", "It reduces the need for indexes"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Normalization organizes database tables to reduce redundancy and improving data integrity. it can lead to a higher number of tables as it breaks down larger tables to eliminate redundancy', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1211, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01212', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is a key advantage of denormalization in a data warehouse?', '["Minimizing storage space usage", "Reducing data redundancy", "Improving query performance for read-heavy operations", "Eliminating complex joins between tables", "Ensuring strict ACID compliance"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Denormalization increases storage due to data redundancy. Option 2: Incorrect. Denormalization increases redundancy. Option 3: Correct. Denormalization speeds up read-heavy queries by reducing joins. Option 4: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1212, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01213', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL command would remove all rows from a table called orders without deleting the table itself?', '["DROP TABLE", "DELETE TABLE", "DELETE FROM", "TRUNCATE TABLE", "REMOVE FROM"]'::jsonb, 3, 'DROP TABLE This command deletes the entire table along with its structure and all the rows inside it. The table would no longer exist in the database. it is incorrect. 2) DELETE TABLE This is not a valid SQL syntax', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1213, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01214', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What does the srcset attribute in an <img> tag achieve?', '["Defines fallback content for unsupported images. iydh fkdolajk", "Specifies multiple image sources for different screen resolutions or sizes", "Automatically compresses images for faster loading", "Links the image to its description", "Associates the image with a style rule"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) Specifies multiple image sources for different screen resolutions or sizes. The srcset attribute in an conditions under which each image should be such as varying screen resolutions or display sizes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1214, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01215', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following is an advantage of creating a SQL constraint with a kula SQL jdis fudkjdo@ A. Ease of applying a constraint to multiple fields at myiq Ease of removal of constraint', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "Both A and B A B hk", "All C. C"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Statement This is correct. When you define a named it explicitly identifies a rule that applies to a combination of such as for a composite primary key or a unique constraint', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1215, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01216', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'In database what is the use of form validations?', '["To allow faster updates", "To restrict invalid data entry", "To speed up SQL queries", "To remove data duplicates", "To generate automated backups"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In database form validations are used primarily to restrict invalid data entry. When users input data into validations ensure that the data adheres to specific or thereby preventing errors or incorrect data f rom being stored in the database', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1216, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01217', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What does the preload attribute in the <video> and <audio> tags do?', '["Specifies whether the browser should load the entire media before playback", "Optimizes the video for faster loading", "Controls buffering options for better streaming", "Preloads a fallback version of the media", "Defines a custom script for media loading"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This is one of the functions of the preload attribute. It helps determine how much of the media file is fetched before starting playback. preload Option 2: This is not the exact purpose of the preload attribute', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1217, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01218', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What happens when you perform an inner join between two tables without any matching rows?', '["The result will include all rows from both tables", "The result will include unmatched rows as NULL", "No rows will be returned", "Only rows from the left table will be included", "An error will be thrown"]'::jsonb, 3, 'When performing an inner join between two tables without any matching no rows will be returned. An inner join only returns rows where there is a match in both tables based on the specified condition (e.g., matching values in a column)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1218, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01219', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL operator is used to check whether a value is within a specific range?', '["LIKE", "BETWEEN", "IN", "EXISTS", "ISNULL"]'::jsonb, 2, 'LIKE This operator is used for pattern not for checking a range. It''s typically used with wildcards like % to match similar patterns in strings. operator mrdihla iudk rgd 2) BETWEEN Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1219, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01220', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'How does the download attribute in the <a> tag function?', '["Automatically opens the linked file in a new tab. ine\u00a2 kj tll iajhxl%Shj", "Forces the browser to download the linked file instead of navigating to it", "Specifies the file''s size for download", "Validates the file''s content before downloading", "Restricts the file to local storage only"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) Forces the browser to download the linked file instead of navigating to it. The download attribute in the it or navigating to it', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1220, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01221', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the correct order of execution in an SQL query?', '["SELECT \u2192 FROM \u2192 WHERE \u2192 GROUP BY \u2192 HAVING \u2192 ORDER BY", "WHERE \u2192 FROM \u2192 SELECT \u2192 ORDER BY \u2192 GROUP BY \u2192 HAVING", "FROM \u2192 WHERE \u2192 GROUP BY \u2192 HAVING \u2192 SELECT \u2192 ORDER BY", "GROUP BY \u2192 SELECT \u2192 WHERE \u2192 FROM \u2192 HAVING \u2192 ORDER BY", "ORDER BY \u2192 WHERE \u2192 GROUP BY \u2192 HAVING \u2192 FROM \u2192 SELECT"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct order of execution in an SQL query is from which identifies the tables or followed by WHERE to filter then GROUP BY to group the and HA VING to filter those groups', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1221, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01222', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which join will retrieve all rows from the left table and the matched rows from the right table?', '["Inner Join", "Full Outer Join", "Right Outer Join", "Left Outer Join", "Self Join"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The Left Outer Join retrieves all rows from the left table and the matched rows from the right table. If there is no match in the right table for a row in the left the result will still include the left table''s with NULL values for the columns of the right table', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1222, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01223', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL command can be used to copy data from one table to another?', '["COPY", "INSERT INTO ... SELECT", "SELECT INTO", "Both 2 and 3", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The SQL command used to copy data from one table to another can be either INSERT INTO ... SELECT or SELECT INTO. The INSERT INTO ... SELECT command allows you to insert the results of a query into an existing while SELECT INTO creates a new table and copies the data into it', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1223, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01224', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which command is used to remove a stored procedure from the database?', '["DELETE PROCEDURE", "DROP PROCEDURE", "REMOVE PROCEDURE", "ALTER PROCEDURE", "TRUNCATE PROCEDURE"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "DROP PROCEDURE". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1224, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01225', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What does the WITH keyword do in SQL?', '["Defines a temporary named result set (Common Table Expression)", "Creates a new table", "Updates rows in a table", "Specifies constraints for a column", "Grants permissions to a user"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Defines a temporary named result set (Common Table Expression)". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1225, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01226', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What happens in a delete anomaly?', '["Unnecessary data is inserted", "Non-relevant data cannot be retrieved", "Deleting a record may remove other important data", "Data is updated inconsistently", "Tables are unable to delete foreign key values. j.="]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is 3) Deleting a record may remove other important data. A delete anomaly occurs when the deletion of a record inadvertently results in the loss of other valuable or essential information', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1226, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01227', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which statement is true about a TRIGGER in SQL?', '["It is executed manually", "It cannot perform INSERT operations", "It is automatically invoked by specific database events", "It can be associated with multiple tables at the same time. th j.= lsysmhla", "It is part of the SQL standard syntax for VIEW. th SQL"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is 3) It is automatically invoked by specific database events. A trigger in SQL is a database object that is automatically executed or invoked when a specified event occurs in the database. These events can include or DELETE operations', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1227, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01228', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'In first normal form (1NF), which condition is mandatory?', '["No duplicate rows", "Each table must have a foreign key", "Data must be stored in separate columns with atomic values", "Tables must eliminate transitive dependencies", "Each table must have composite keys"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In 1NF (First Normal Form), the following conditions must be 1NF • Atomic Values Each column must contain single values (not lists or sets). • No Repeating Groups The table should not contain multiple values in a single column or repeating columns for similar data. j', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1228, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01229', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What will the query SELECT COUNT(*) FROM return?', '["The number of rows in the including NULL values. NULL", "The number of rows in the excluding NULL values", "The number of non-NULL columns in the table", "The total size of the table in bytes", "The maximum value in the table"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The given code initializes i to -1 and sum_val to 0, and then enters a while loop that continues as long as i is greater than -10. Within the if i is its value is added to and if i is its value is subtracted from sum_val. After each i is decremented by 1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1229, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01230', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL statement is used to add a new column to an existing table?', '["UPDATE TABLE table_name ADD COLUMN column_name", "INSERT INTO table_name ADD COLUMN column_name", "ALTER TABLE table_name ADD COLUMN column_name", "MODIFY TABLE table_name ADD column_name", "SELECT ADD COLUMN column_name datatype FROM"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In to add a new column to an existing use the ALTER TABLE statement with the ADD COLUMN clause. SQL ALTER TABLE table_name ADD COLUMN column_name • table_name The name of the existing table. • column_name The name of the new column', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1230, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01231', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What does the following SQL query do ?', '["It selects all records where the price is greater than 50, sorted by the date column in ascending order", "It selects all records where the price is greater than 50, sorted by the date column in descending order", "It selects all records with a price less than or equal to 50, ordered by date in descending order. th 50 g wvq iudk", "It deletes records where the price is greater than 50", "It updates records where the price is greater than 50 to set the date column in descending order"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The given SQL query retrieves all rows from the table where the is greater than 50. This is achieved using the *` statement to fetch all columns and the clause to filter rows based on the condition processing. ,nd lr', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1231, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01232', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL statement is used to enforce referential integrity between tables?', '["PRIMARY KEY", "FOREIGN KEY", "CHECK", "UNIQUE", "DEFAULT"]'::jsonb, 2, 'PRIMARY KEY Ensures uniqueness within a table but does not enforce relationships between tables. 2) FOREIGN KEY It is used to enforce referential integrity by ensuring that a value in one table corresponds to a valid value in another table. w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1232, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01233', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following SQL statements is used to insert a new record into a table students with columns name and age?', '["INSERT INTO students VALUES (''John'',", "INSERT INTO students age) VALUES (''John'',", "INSERT NEW INTO students age) VALUES (''John'',", "INSERT INTO students (''name'', ''age'') VALUES (''John'',", "INSERT INTO students VALUES (name = ''John'', age ="]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct SQL statement to insert a new record into the table with specific columns and INSERT INTO students age) VALUES (''John'', This statement explicitly specifies the columns into which values should be ensuring the data aligns correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1233, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01234', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What will be the output of this query?', '["It will return all the cities from the customers including duplicates. th", "It will return only distinct cities (no duplicates) from the customers table. th k.r", "It will return all the customers from the customers with duplicates. th", "It will return the total number of cities in the customers table. th", "It will delete all cities from the customers table. th k.r uld oukq"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) It will return only distinct cities (no duplicates) from the customers table. The SELECT DISTINCT query ensures that only unique values from the specified column in this case) are eliminating any duplicate entries from the result set. ,nd fokq w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1234, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01235', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What would be the best reason to use a FULL OUTER JOIN in a database query?', '["To combine all records from two even those without matches in either table. j.= foll", "To combine only matching records from two tables. j.= follska", "To combine all records from the first table and matching ones from the second", "To exclude records with NULL values. NULL", "To create a cross-product of two tables. j.= foll"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "To combine all records from two even those without matches in either table. j.= foll". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1235, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01236', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL query retrieves unique records from a table?', '["SELECT DISTINCT", "SELECT UNIQUE", "SELECT RECORDS", "SELECT ROWS", "SELECT FILTER"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is 1) SELECT DISTINCT because this query is specifically designed to retrieve unique records from a table by eliminating duplicate rows. When is the database ensures that only one occurrence of each unique record is returned in the result set', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1236, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01237', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is a primary key in a relational database?', '["A key that uniquely identifies a record in a table", "A key that establishes a link between records in two tables. j.= foll", "A key used for encrypting data in a table", "A key that indexes the data in a table", "A key that maintains data integrity in a table"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The primary key in a relational database is a key that uniquely identifies a record in a table. It ensures that each record can be distinctively accessed and preventing duplicate entries', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1237, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01238', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What will happen if the UPDATE statement is executed without a WHERE clause?', '["Only the first row is updated", "All rows in the table are updated", "No rows are updated", "An error is returned", "Only the column values are updated"]'::jsonb, 2, 'If the UPDATE statement is executed without a WHERE all rows in the table will be updated. The WHERE clause specifies the condition for selecting rows that should be modified. Without the operation applies to every updating the specified c olumn(s) with the provided values', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1238, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01239', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which constraint enforces the uniqueness of a column in a table?', '["CHECK", "UNIQUE", "FOREIGN KEY", "NOT NULL", "DEFAULT"]'::jsonb, 2, 'CHECK Restricts values based on a specified condition but does not enforce uniqueness. 2) UNIQUE The UNIQUE constraint ensures that all values in a column are preventing duplicate entries. It enforces uniqueness but allows NULL values unless specified otherwise. UNIQUE w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1239, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01240', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Normalization in database design helps', '["Increase redundancy in data", "Reduce data integrity", "Organize data into efficient structures", "Speed up database queries", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Organize data into efficient structures". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1240, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
