('alict_01283', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the difference between INNER JOIN and OUTER JOIN?', '["INNER JOIN returns all OUTER JOIN returns only matching rows. INNER JOIN", "INNER JOIN returns only matching OUTER JOIN returns all rows from both tables. INNER JOIN ,nd fokafka", "INNER JOIN returns only matching rows from both OUTER JOIN returns all rows from one table and matching rows from the other. INNER JOIN j.= foflkau", "INNER JOIN returns distinct OUTER JOIN returns duplicate rows. INNER JOIN", "There is no difference"]'::jsonb, 3, 'INNER JOIN This type of JOIN returns only rows with matching values in both tables. If there is no match between the those rows are excluded. wdldrfha JOIN j.= foflysu OUTER JOIN This JOIN type includes rows from one table even if they do not have matching rows in the other table', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1283, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01284', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following SQL statements correctly selects all records from a table named Employees where the column Salary is from 50000 to 100000?', '["SELECT * FROM Employees WHERE Salary = 50000 TO", "SELECT * FROM Employees WHERE Salary BETWEEN 50000 AND", "SELECT * FROM Employees WHERE Salary", "SELECT * FROM Employees WHERE Salary NOT BETWEEN 50000 AND", "SELECT * FROM Employees WHERE Salary IS BETWEEN 50000 AND"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. The syntax = 50000 TO 100000 is not valid in SQL', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1284, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01285', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Consider the following SQL AVG(salary) FROM employees GROUP BY department HAVING AVG(salary) > will this query do?', '["It will return the departments where the total salary is greater than th jegqm 50\"000 g", "It will return the departments where the average salary is greater than jegqm 50\"000 g", "It will return all departments regardless of salary. jegqm", "It will return only employees with a salary greater than th 50\"000 g", "It will return the salary of each including those with an average less than th jegqm 50\"000 g wvq wh"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The query calculates the average salary for each department using AVG(salary). The GROUP BY department groups the employees by their department. GROUP BY department fiajlhska Tjqkaf', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1285, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01286', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Consider the following CSS selectors and their CSS jrl tajdfha ld¾hhka #main-content h1 1px solid .highlight of the following statements correctly identifies the type of each selector?', '["A is an Element B is a Class C is an ID D is an Attribute selector. A", "A is an ID B is an Element C is an Attribute D is a Class selector A", "A is a Class B is an Element C is an Attribute D is an ID selector A", "A is an ID B is an Attribute C is an Element D is a Class selector A", "A is a Class B is an ID C is an Attribute D is an Element selector A"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "A is an ID B is an Element C is an Attribute D is a Class selector A". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1286, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01287', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which SQL keyword is used to sort the result set of a SQL query?', '["GROUP BY", "ORDER BY", "SORT", "FILTER", "ARRANGE"]'::jsonb, 2, 'GROUP BY This is used to group rows that have the same values in specified columns. It is not used for sorting. GROUP BY Class groups data based on the Class column', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1287, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01288', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'RegNo) What is the correct SQL code to insert the foreign key into the Section table above?', '["INSERT TABLE Section ADD FOREIGN KEY", "ALTER TABLE Section ADD FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES", "ALTER TABLE Section ADD FOREIGN KEY", "ALTER TABLE Student ADD FOREIGN KEY", "INSERT INTO Section ADD PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES"]'::jsonb, 2, 'This SQL command does the following SQL ALTER TABLE Section Modifies the Section table. ADD FOREIGN KEY Adds a foreign key constraint to the column. REFERENCES Student(RegNo) Links this column to the column in the Student table (which is assumed to be a primary key)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1288, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01289', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which attribute of the <option> element specifies the value that will be sent to the server when the form is submitted?', '["label This statement is false. The label attribute is used to define the visible text of the", "value This statement is true. The value attribute of the", "text This statement is false. There is n o text attribute for", "id This statement is false. The id attribute is used to uniquely identify an element within the document and is not related to the form submission values", "content This statement is false. There is no content attribute for"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "label This statement is false. The label attribute is used to define the visible text of the". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1289, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01290', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the purpose of the SQL "GROUP BY" clause?', '["Filtering records based on specified conditions", "Sorting records in ascending order", "Deleting duplicate records from a table", "Grouping rows that have the same values into summary rows. tlu", "Modifying existing records in a table"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Grouping rows that have the same values into summary rows. tlu". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1290, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01291', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which attribute of the <input> element ensures that a user must enter data into the field before submitting the form?', '["required According to this it''s true. The required attribute ensures that a user must enter data into the field before submitting the form. It makes the field mandatory for form submission. th", "mandatory According to this it''s false. There is no mandatory attribute in for", "validate According to this it''s false. The validate attribute does not exist for", "validate-required According to this it''s false. There is no validate-required attribute for", "validate-input According to this it''s false. The validate-input attribute does not exist. The required attribute is used to ensure that a user must enter data before form submission. th"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "required According to this it''s true. The required attribute ensures that a user must enter data into the field before submitting the form. It makes the field mandatory for form submission. th". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1291, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
