('alict_01293', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Consider the following code src = "moon.jpg" alt = "moon" width = "300" height = The above code line renders the image named "moon.jpg" by the u.ska "moon.jpg" lr The browser knows the size (width and height) of the without width and Wi& The alt attribute provides alternative information for image if a user for some reason cannot view ksid th fkdyels alt imhhs'' Which of the above statements are o@ Answer : 4) Statement', '["A and B only. A B", "A and C only. A C", "B and C only. B C", "All of the above", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A and B only. A B". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1293, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01294', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Select the correct statement about the following SQL query', '["Retrieves the \"first_name\" and \"last_name\" of employees hired in the year 2024, and sorts the results by \"hire_date\" in descending order. 2024", "Retrieves the \"first_name\" and \"last_name\" of employees and sorts the results by \"first_name\" in ascending order. fiajlhskaf.a \"first_name\" \"last_name\" ,nd fok", "Retrieves the \"first_name\" and \"last_name\" of employees hired in the year 2023, and sorts the results by \"hire_date\" in descending order. 2023", "Retrieves the \"first_name\" and \"last_name\" of employees hired in the year 2023, and sorts the results by \"hire_date\" in ascending order. 2023", "Retrieves the \"first_name\" and \"last_name\" of employees hired outside the year 2023, and sorts the results by \"hire_date\" in ascending order. 2023 jifrka"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The Python code initializes i = 1 and j = 10, then enters a while loop that runs as long as i is less than j. In each if i is even (i % 2 == 0), j is decreased by 2. This process continues until i is no longer less than j', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1294, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
