('alict_01298', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following can be used to identify each row of the table uniquely?', '["FOREIGN KEY", "DISTINCT KEY", "PRIMARY KEY", "UNIQUE KEY", "NULL KEY"]'::jsonb, 3, 'FOREIGN This is used to establish and enforce a link between the data in two tables. It refers to the primary key of another table and is used to maintain referential integrity. j.= foll 1) A only. A 2) B only. B 3) A and B only. A B 4) A and C only. A C', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1298, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
