('alict_01351', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following scenarios best demonstrates a "Many-to-Many" relationship between two tables in a relational database?', '["A customer can place many and each order is placed by one fndfyda", "An author can write many and a book can be written by many", "An employee can be assigned to one and a department can have many employees ''", "A student can have one and a mentor can have many yels", "A company has one and the CEO manages many iud.ulg m%Odk"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is a One-to-Many relationship (one customer can place multiple but each order belongs to only one customer). -nyq', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1351, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01352', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which attribute sets the initial value of an input element ?', '["name", "value", "type", "placeholder", "initial"]'::jsonb, 2, 'fukak 1) The name attribute is used to specify the name of the input element. This name is used to reference the input field''s data when the form is submitted. It does not set the initial value of the input field', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1352, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01353', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Consider the following SQL department FROM employees WHERE department = does this query do?', '["It inserts new rows into the employees table for the Sales department. th Sales", "It updates the department of employees to ''Sales''. th employees", "It deletes employees from the Sales department. th Sales", "It selects the employee and department of employees who work in the Sales department. th Sales", "It joins the employees table with another table. th employees"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: According to this it is false. The query does not insert new rows into the employees table. It only retrieves data from the table. Option 2: According to this it is false. The query does not update the department of employees', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1353, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01354', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'How does Geographic Information System (GIS) differ from a traditional database system?', '["GIS is specialized in storing and analyzing spatial and geographical whereas traditional databases handle numerical and textual data without a spatial component. GIS", "Traditional databases are used for while GIS is only used for real -time applications", "GIS focuses on business while traditional databases focus on customer service. GIS", "Traditional databases are used in while GIS is not used for any commercial purpose", "GIS is limited to natural resources while traditional databases are used for all industries. GIS"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: GIS is a specialized system designed to and visualize spatial and geographical data regions). It uses and spatial analysis techniques to study and trends in geographical contexts', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1354, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01355', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the purpose of the SQL WHERE clause?', '["Specify the order of results", "Filter rows based on a condition", "Join multiple tables", "Grouping rows together", "Perform mathematical calculations on the selected columns"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Filter rows based on a condition". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1355, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01356', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following is an example of a "Many-to-Many" relationship in a relational database?', '["A student can enroll in many and each course can have many students fndfyda", "A car has one owner", "A single customer can place many orders. fndfyda", "A manager can manage only one department", "A city has many zip codes"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This is the best example of a Many -to-Many relationship. In a this relationship is often implemented using a join table "Enrollments") that links the primary key of the Students table with the primary key of the Courses table. isiqka j', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1356, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01357', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'The school table shows the teachers in a school and the subjects they teach. What is the correct SQL code related to its selection of different subjects in the subject column?', '["SELECT LIKE subject FROM", "SELECT * FROM school WHERE", "SELECT DISTINCT school FROM", "SELECT * FROM school IN", "SELECT DISTINCT subject FROM"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "SELECT DISTINCT subject FROM". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1357, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01358', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the SQL code delete the Alab?', '["drop", "drop database", "delete", "delete database", "remove datacase"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "drop database". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1358, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01359', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'A student''s name has 3 parts namely First Middle Name and Last Name. What type of attribute does this belong to?', '["Derived Attributes", "Single Valued Attributes", "Multi Valued Attributes", "Composite Attributes", "Stored Attributes"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Derived Attributes These are attributes whose values are calculated or derived from other attributes. For an "Age" attribute might be derived from a "Date of Birth" attribute. Date of Birth A student''s name is not derived from other', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1359, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01360', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the correct SQL statement to delete a database called ''School''?', '["delete", "delete database", "drop", "drop database", "remove database"]'::jsonb, 4, 'In the correct statement to delete a database is "DROP DATABASE command is specifically designed to remove an entire including all its and stored procedures. The keyword DROP is used in SQL to permanently delete objects such as or views', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1360, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01361', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following SQL queries will update the "Brand" column to "Samsung" for all records in the "Products" table where the "ProductCategory" is "Phone"?', '["UPDATE Products SET Brand = IF ProductCategory =", "MODIFY Products SET Brand = WHERE ProductCategory =", "UPDATE Products SET Brand = WHERE ProductCategory =", "ALTER TABLE Products SET Brand = WHERE ProductCategory =", "UPDATE Products MODIFY Brand = WHERE ProductCategory ="]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "UPDATE Products SET Brand = WHERE ProductCategory =". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1361, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01362', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following statements is true about the UNION operator in SQL?', '["It combines the results of two SELECT statements and retains duplicates. th SELECT foll", "It combines the results of two SELECT statements but removes duplicates. th SELECT foll", "It merges rows with identical columns and orders them by default. th", "It is the same as INNER JOIN. th INNER JOIN iudk", "It can only be used with SELECT statements having different numbers of columns. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: False. The UNION operator automatically removes duplicates unless UNION ALL is used. Option 2: True. The UNION operator merges the results of two SELECT statements and eliminates duplicate rows. Option 3: False', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1362, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01363', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the most correct and convenient SQL statement that will update Building of Faculty of IT to "B7"?', '["UPDATE employees SET Building = ''B7'' WHERE Name IN (''Bkon'',", "UPDATE employees SET Building = ''B7'' WHERE Building =", "UPDATE employees SET Building = ''B7'' WHERE FacultyCode =", "UPDATE employees SET Building = ''B7'' WHERE City IN (''Kurunegala'',", "UPDATE employees SET Building = ''B7'' WHERE IN (10001,"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This relies on specific which may not be reliable or scalable. Incorrect because the update should target Faculty of not specific names. Option 2: This updates all rows with Building "B4", which includes rows not related to Faculty of IT', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1363, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01364', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following database system model is in accordance with Parent-Child relationship in data processing?', '["Structural", "Object Oriented", "Hierarchical", "Network", "Relational"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 2: This focuses on storing data as objects with attributes and methods. Option 1: This is Not a standard database Option 3: The Hierarchical Database Model organizes data in a tree -like where each record has a single parent and potentially multiple children', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1364, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01365', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Below is a table with details of students of a school. What is the correct SQL code to change the Kavindu''s class to 12A?', '["UPDATE student ALTER class = WHERE id = 002", "UPDATE student SET class = WHERE id = 002", "INSERT INTO student ALTER class = WHERE id = 002", "UPDATE student SET class = WHERE", "UPDATE student SELECT class = WHERE id = 002"]'::jsonb, 2, 'This is the correct SQL command to modify existing records in a table. (in this student) Specifies the column to be updated (in this '' 12A'') and the new value to assign', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1365, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01366', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Consider the following table representing Employees. Employees Name Department Salary 1001 Alice IT 4500 1002 Bob HR 3500 1003 Charlie IT 5500 Which SQL command will retrieve the average salary of employees in the IT department?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "D only. D", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The correct function for calculating the average is AVG(). .Kkh Statement SELECT AVG(Salary) FROM Employees WHERE Department = the correct syntax by applying the AVG function to the Salary column and filtering rows where the Department is ''IT''', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1366, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01367', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following best describes the purpose of a DFD?', '["To model data structures", "To represent the flow of data within a system", "To depict the physical structure of a database", "To describe user interface layouts", "To show how a system will be implemented"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. A Data Flow Diagram (DFD) doesn''t model data structures. Data structures are about how data is organized and stored in which is typically represented using techniques like entity - relationship diagrams or class not', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1367, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01368', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following is a commonly used platform for building e-commerce websites?', '["Photoshop", "Excel", "Shopify", "Microsoft Word", "SQL"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Shopify". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1368, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01369', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following describes a "virtual storefront"?', '["A physical store that operates", "An online platform where businesses display and sell their", "A service that provides virtual reality", "A database used for managing e-commerce .kqfokq", "A software tool for designing"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2). A "virtual storefront" refers to an online platform that functions similarly to a physical store but exists only on the internet', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1369, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01370', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'A hospital is developing a patient management system. Consider the following frda.S ixj¾Okh The system must allow doctors to update patient medical ffjoHjrekag frda.Skaf.a bv The system must ensure data encryption for all patient frda.S Nurses should be able to schedule appointments for frda.Ska yels The system must be accessible 24', '["1, 3,", "2,", "1, 2,", "2, 3,", "1, 4,"]'::jsonb, 1, 'In this the functional requirements are 1, 3, and 5 because they describe specific tasks or services the system must transferring viewing transaction and generating statements. These define what the system does', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1370, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01371', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'The end of a file is indicated by -1 and the size of one group in the table is 4KB. According to the above what is the starting batch number and file size of the larger capacity file?', '["203, 24KB", "202, 20KB", "210, 20KB", "207, 28KB", "203, 16KB"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "210, 20KB". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1371, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01372', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'The operation of the above circuit is similar to which of the following gates?', '["AND gate", "OR gate", "NAND gate", "NOR gate", "XOR gate"]'::jsonb, 5, 'we will record the outputs given by each gate according to its input as follows and obtain the final output. wjika The final output A̅. B + A. B̅ is the output of the XOR gate. fuys wjidk', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1372, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01373', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Assume that you need to build a logic circuit for the edge lighting feature when a notification is received this effect will only work if the screen is turned off. What''s the best logic gate to the above -mentioned scenario?', '["OR gate", "NOT gate", "NOR gate", "AND gate", "NAND gate"]'::jsonb, 4, 'we need to check both a notification is received and whether the screen is turned off. an AND gate is the best option to check these conditions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1373, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01374', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which logic gate does the following logic circuit equals iudk 5) Explanation', '["NAND Gate", "OR Gate", "NOR Gate", "XOR Gate", "AND Gate"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "NAND Gate". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1374, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01375', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is the logic gate that has a similar function to the one in the circuit below?', '["AND", "OR", "NOT", "XOR", "XNOR Explanation"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Switch as Input - ON - "1" - OFF - "0" XNOR', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1375, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01376', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider the Boolean expression given olajd = 1B + (1B + CD)C Which of the following is the most simplified expression for the above Boolean expression Y?', '["B + CB + D", "B + CD", "1", "CD + B\u0305", "B"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Let''s solve Y = 1B + (1B + CD)C using Boolean = 1B + (1B + CD) C = B + (B + CD) C Identity law = B + CB + CCD Distributive law = B + CB + CD Idempotent law = B + CD Redundancy law', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1376, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01377', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Simplify the following Boolean expression', '["K", "K + J", "K + J. L", "0", "KL + LJ"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "K + J. L". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1377, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01378', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is the POS expression equivalent to following SOP expression', '["(P\u0305 + Q + R\u0305). (P\u0305 + Q + R). (P + Q + R\u0305). (P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R). (P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R\u0305)", "(P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R\u0305). (P\u0305 + Q + R). (P\u0305 + Q + R\u0305). (P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R). (P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R\u0305)", "(P + Q\u0305 + R). (P + Q\u0305 + R\u0305). (P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R). (P + Q + R\u0305). (P + Q + R)", "(P\u0305 + Q + R\u0305) + (P\u0305 + Q + R) + (P + Q + R\u0305) + (P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R) + (P\u0305 + Q\u0305 + R\u0305)", "(P\u0305QR\u0305) + (P\u0305QR) + (PQR\u0305) + (P\u0305Q\u0305R) + (P\u0305Q\u0305R\u0305)"]'::jsonb, 1, 'First to convert a SOP to the whole expression must be given in the negative form. For that we first put a bar to the whole expression. SOP tlla POS PQ̅R + PQ̅R̅ + P̅Q̅R + PQR̅ + PQR̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ Then we apply De Morgan''s law (PQ̅R̅̅̅̅̅̅ ). (PQ̅R̅̅̅̅̅̅̅)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1378, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01379', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'In a Full Adder what will be the outputs if the inputs are A = 0, B = 1, and Carry in = 1?', '["Sum = 0, Carry out = 1", "Sum = 0, Carry out = 0", "Sum = 1, Carry out = 0", "Sum = 1, Carry out = 1", "Not enough data to calculate. .Kkh"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Sum = 0, Carry out = 1". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1379, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01380', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Simplify the following Boolean lrkak. (J + K). (K + L). (J + K + 3) Let''s simplify the given Boolean lruq'' = (J + K). (K + L + 0). (J + K + L) Identity Law', '["K", "K + J", "K + J. L", "0", "KL + LJ"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "K". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1380, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01381', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider the given Boolean ,nd', '["AC + AB", "A + BC", "AB + C", "B(A + C)", "A(B + C)"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "B(A + C)". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1381, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01382', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is the simplified form of the following Boolean expression?', '["231310", "218710", "245610", "223310", "234710"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "231310". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1382, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01383', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following is incorrect about Karnaugh Maps (K-map)?', '["It is used to minimize Boolean expressions. th", "Groups of ones can only be made in powers of 2. yelafla 2fla", "Only the adjacent ones in a K-map can be grouped", "The ones in a corner cannot form a group with other ones", "Groups can wrap around the edges of the K-map"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Correct. K-maps are a tool used to simplify or minimize Boolean expressions by grouping adjacent ones in the map. This helps in reducing the complexity of digital circuits. wju Option 2: Correct. In a the groups of adjacent ones can only be of size 1, 2, 4, 8, etc', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1383, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01384', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What gate is indicated by this circuit?', '["OR gate", "AND gate", "NAND gate", "NOR gate", "XOR gate"]'::jsonb, 4, 'According to this when one switch is turned the bulb does not light. when both switches are turned it does not light up. The reason is that the circuit is shorted when the switches are turned on. But when both switches are left the bulb lights up normally', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1384, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01385', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'In order to study under the advanced level commerce stream of a students must study accounting (A) and economics (B) subjects. Business studies(C) or ICT(D) can be chosen as third subject. What is the appropriate Boolean expression for this?', '["A+B+(C+D)", "AB(C+D)", "A+B+(CD)", "AB(CD)", "AB+(C+D)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'a student must study both A and B. That means A and B are connected with an AND gate. (A. B) oajdrhla After only one of the subjects C and D must be done. That means C and D are connected with an OR gate', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1385, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01386', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following is the correct standard expression of the given non-standard SOP expression?', '["P. Q. R + P. Q. R\u0305 + P. Q\u0305. R\u0305 + P\u0305. Q. R", "P. Q. R + P. Q. R + P. Q. R\u0305 + P\u0305. Q. R", "P. Q. R\u0305 + P. Q. R\u0305 + P. Q\u0305. R\u0305 + P\u0305. Q. R", "P. Q. R + P. Q. R\u0305 + P. Q\u0305. R\u0305 + P\u0305. Q. R\u0305", "P. Q\u0305. R + P. Q. R\u0305 + P. Q\u0305. R\u0305 + P\u0305. Q. R"]'::jsonb, 1, 'FSOP = P. Q + P. R̅ + Q. R = P. Q. 1 + P. R̅. 1 + Q. R. 1 Identity law = P. Q. (R + R̅) + P. R̅. (Q + Q̅) + Q. R. (P + P̅) Inverse law = P. Q. R + P. Q. R̅ + P. Q. R̅ + P. Q̅. R̅ + P. Q. R + P̅. Q. R Distributive law = P. Q. R + P. Q. R̅ + P. Q. R̅ + P. Q̅. R̅ + P̅. Q', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1386, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01387', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following statements is true regarding the behavior of circuits?', '["A combinational circuit produces an output based on both the current and previous inputs. ixfhdack", "A Full Adder adds two bits using XOR to produce a sum and carry out XOR folla lr", "A flip-flop is a combinational circuit that outputs a result based on both current and previous inputs", "A Half Adder produces a sum and carry out bits but cannot handle carry in", "A sequential circuit operates only based on the current inputs"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Incorrect. A combinational circuit is a type of circuit where the output is determined by the current inputs. It does not have memory meaning the output depends only on the present values of the and not on any past values or previous states. Option 2: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1387, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01388', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider the following logic circuit which involves multiple gates. If the input A = 1, B = 0, and C = will be the output of the expression?', '["0", "1", "2", "Undefined", "3"]'::jsonb, 1, 'let''s replace the Boolean variables with the given values. A AND B = 1 AND 0 = 0 NOT C AND A = NOT 1 AND 1 = 0 AND 1 = 0 B XOR C = 0 XOR 1 = 1 let''s do the complete Boolean simplification 0 OR 0 AND 1 = 0', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1388, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01389', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'In a security three sensors B and C output 1 when detecting motion and 0 when not. The alarm activates based B C 1o tfia jkafka" • If Sensor A detects a the alarm activates. A If Sensor A does not detect the alarm will activate if Sensor B detects motion and Sensor C does not detect motion. A y÷kd fkd.kafka B y÷kd .kafka C y÷kd fkd.kafka If Sensor A and Sensor B do not detect the alarm does not regardless of Sensor C A B fkdlrkafka C Boolean expression correctly represents the alarm activation?', '["A", "A + A\u0305BC\u0305", "A\u0305BC\u0305 + AC", "A + B", "A + BC\u0305"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Let''s consider the given conditions • According to condition 1, if A the alarm is no matter what the values of B and C are. fldkafoaish 1 g A = 1 • Condition 2 says that if A = 0, the alarm will activate only if B = 1 and C = 0', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1389, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01390', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which gate does the output from the circuit below correspond ,efnk iudk 3) Explanation', '["AND", "OR", "XOR", "XNOR", "NAND Let''s consider the truth tables for each option separately"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "XOR". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1390, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01391', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'A circuit consists of three inputs C) and produces an output of 1 only when an odd number of inputs are 1. Which logic function does it perform?', '["NAND", "XOR", "AND", "NOR", "XNOR"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The XOR (Exclusive OR) function outputs 1 if and only if an odd number of inputs are 1. XOR (Exclusive OR) For a three-input XOR function (A ⊕ B ⊕ C) If one or all three inputs are 1, the output is 1. tlla If zero or two inputs are 1, the output is 0', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1391, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01392', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following Boolean expressions are definitely identical to each other?', '["A only A", "B only B", "A and B only A B", "C and D only C D", "C and D all C D"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Let''s simplify each option given in the question A) = A + BC + B̅ + C̅ = A + C + B̅ + C̅ Redundancy Law = A + B̅ + C̅ + C Commutative Law = A + B̅ + 1 Inverse Law = 1 Identity Law B) = X + XY + ZX + X̅ = X + X̅ + XY + ZX Commutative Law = 1 + XY + ZX Inverse Law = 1 Identity Law C) = M', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1392, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01393', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which statement best describes why NOR gate is called a "universal gate"?', '["It can only implement NOT operations", "It can replace AND gates but not OR gates. thg AND oajdr", "Any Boolean function can be constructed using only NOR gates", "It''s cheaper to manufacture than other gates", "It cannot create complex circuits alone"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A NOR gate is called a "universal gate" because you can build any other type of logic circuit using only NOR gates. This means that if you only have NOR gates you can combine them in different ways to create the functions of gates and so on', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1393, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01394', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What''s the most simplified Boolean expression of the following logic 2) Explanation', '["A + B", "AB\u0305 + C", "A + B + C", "AB", "A + B\u0305C"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A + B". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1394, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01395', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'A smart home system controls lights based on two ksjdi fldkafoais folla myka lrhs( Motion detected (M) - 1 if motion is 0 (M) - 1 tfia 0'' Time of day (N) - 1 if it is 0 (N) - 1" tfia 0'' The lights should turn ON (L = 1) only when either motion is detected OR it is but not both at the same myka (L = 1) folu Boolean expression correctly represents the light control logic?', '["L = M + N", "L = M. N", "L = M \u2295 N", "L = M\u0305 + N", "L = M. N\u0305"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Understanding the logic The light (L) should turn ON (1) • Motion is detected (M = 1) and it is NOT nighttime (N = 0). • It is nighttime (N = 1) and NO motion is detected (M = 0)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1395, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01396', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'A security system is designed to allow access only if both a correct PIN is entered (P) and a valid ID card is scanned (I). if an administrator (A) is access is always granted regardless of the PIN or ID. wdrlaIl lr PIN tlla (P) lr ,nd Bg (A) PIN ,nd fokq of the following Boolean expressions correctly represents the system''s access control logic?', '["P + I + A", "P. I + A", "P. I. A", "(P + I). A", "P + I. A"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This expression allows access if any of the conditions or A) are true. This is incorrect because it would grant access if only the PIN or ID is which contradicts the scenario. fldkafoaishla I A) th PIN ID ,nd Option 2: P', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1396, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01397', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Simplify the following Boolean expression', '["A + BC", "AB + C", "A + BC\u0305", "A + B\u0305C", "AB + C\u0305"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A + BC̅". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1397, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01398', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider the Boolean expression given olajd = 𝐀̅𝐁 + 𝐀𝐂̅ + 𝐁𝐂̅̅̅̅ In which circuit from the following will the output be equal to the given Boolean iudk 2) Explanation', '["4)", "first AND gate gets the inputs B and outputs A. AND oajdrhg B ,efnk A. B second AND gate outputs B. C", "Z outputs A. B. C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305", "Z outputs A + B + C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305", "The first NOR gate gets the inputs B and outputs A + NOR oajdrh B ,nd f.k A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 lrhs. The second NOR gate gets the inputs C and outputs B + C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305. fojk NOR oajdrh C ,nd f.k B + C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 lrhs. The third NOR gate gets the inputs A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 and B + C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 and outputs A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 + B + NOR oajdrh A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 B + C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 ,nd f.k A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 + B + C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 + B + C\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305. = (A + B\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f). (B + C\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f) = (A + B). (B + C) = B + (A. C) Option"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "first AND gate gets the inputs B and outputs A. AND oajdrhg B ,efnk A. B second AND gate outputs B. C". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1398, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01399', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider the following Boolean + A. C̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ Which of the following is', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Step Apply De Morgan''s Theorem B + A. C̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ = B̅. (A. C̅̅̅̅̅) This matches statement I Step Apply De Morgan''s Theorem to (A. C̅̅̅̅̅) B̅. (A. C̅̅̅̅̅) = B̅. (A̅ + C̅) This matches statement II Step Apply the Distributive Law B̅. (A̅ + C̅) = B̅. A̅ + B̅. C̅ This matches statement III', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1399, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01400', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What''s the correct simplified Boolean expression of the below logic 2) Explanation', '["(A. B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305). (C + D\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305)\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f\u033f", "(A. B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305). (C + D\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305)", "(A. B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305). (C. D\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305)", "(A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305). (C + D\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305)", "(A + B\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305) + (C + D\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305) 5"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "(A. B̅̅̅̅̅). (C + D̅̅̅̅̅̅̅)̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿̿". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1400, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
